hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1621","[AI-translation] Anas bin Malik (raziyallahu anhu) se riwayat hai ke Abu Bakr Siddiq (raziyallahu anhu) ne kaha: Main ne mushrikon ke qadmon ko hamaray saron par dekha jabke ham ghaar mein thay. To main ne kaha: Ae Allah ke Rasool! Agar un mein se koi apne qadmon ko dekhay to hamein apne qadmon ke neechay dekh le. To Aap ne farmaya: Ae Abu Bakr! Un do ke baaray mein tumhara kya khayal hai jin ka teesra Allah hai? (Muslim: 7/108). Baab: Aap (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ka qaul ke apni sohbat aur maal mein mujh par sab se zyada ehsaan karnay wala Abu Bakr hai."
"1622","[AI-translation] Abu Sa'id Khudri (raziyallahu anhu) se riwayat hai ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) mimbar par baithay aur farmaya: Aik banda jisay Allah ne duniya ki raunaq aur apne paas jo hai us ke darmiyan ikhtiyar diya to us ne jo Us ke paas hai usay ikhtiyar kiya. To Abu Bakr (raziyallahu anhu) roye aur roye aur kaha, Muslim mein hai ke kaha: Ham tum par apne maan baap qurban karein. Unhon ne kaha: To Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) hi ikhtiyar diye gaye thay aur Abu Bakr ham mein usay sab se zyada jannay walay thay. Aur Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne farmaya: Beshak apne maal aur apni sohbat mein mujh par sab se zyada ehsaan karnay wala Abu Bakr hai. Aur agar main kisi ko khalil banata to Abu Bakr ko khalil banata, lekin Islam ka bhai chara hai. Masjid mein Abu Bakr ki khirkhi ke siwa koi khirkhi baaqi na rahay. (Muslim: 7/108). Baab: Nabi (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ko sab se pyaray Abu Bakr Siddiq (raziyallahu anhu) hain."
"1623","[AI-translation] Abu Usman se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Mujhe Amr bin Aas ne bataya ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne unhein Zaat-us-Salasil ke lashkar par bheja. To main Aap ke paas aaya aur kaha: Logon mein Aap ko sab se pyara kaun hai? Aap ne farmaya: Aisha. Main ne kaha: Mardon mein se? Aap ne farmaya: Us ka baap. Main ne kaha: Phir kaun? Muslim mein summa nahi hai. Aap ne farmaya: Umar. Phir Aap ne mardon ko ginwaya. (Muslim: 7/109). Baab: Siddiq ke liye nekiyon ke kaam jama hona aur us mein jannat mein dakhil hona; is mein Abu Huraira ki hadees hai jo zakat mein 543 number par guzar chuki hai. Baab: Aap (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ke qaul ke baaray mein ke beshak main us par iman rakhta hun, main aur Abu Bakr aur Umar."
"1624","[AI-translation] Abu Huraira (raziyallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne farmaya: Jabke aik mard apni gaaye hank raha tha jis par us ne bojh lada hua tha, gaaye ne us ki taraf dekha aur kaha ke main is liye paida nahi hui, balke main to khaiti ke liye paida hui hun. To logon ne taajjub aur darr se kaha ke SubhanAllah, gaaye baat karti hai. To Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne farmaya ke beshak main us baat ko sach janta hun aur Abu Bakr aur Umar bhi sach jantay hain. Aik charwaha apni bakriyon mein tha, itnay mein aik bhediya jhapta aur aik bakri le gaya. Charwahay ne us ka peecha kiya aur bakri ko us se chhura liya to bhediye ne us ki taraf dekha aur kaha ke us din bakri ko kaun bachaye ga jis din mere siwa koi charwaha na hoga. Logon ne kaha SubhanAllah! Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne farmaya ke beshak main us ko sach janta hun aur Abu Bakr aur Umar bhi sach jantay hain. Doosri riwayat mein hai ke Abu Bakr aur Umar (raziyallahu anhuma) mojood na thay. Is hadees se un ki bari fazilat nikli ke Aap (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ko un par aisa bharosa tha ke jo baat Aap mantay hain wo bhi zaroor manein ge. (Muslim mein ana nahi hai.)"
"1625","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas (raziyallahu anhuma) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Umar bin Khattab (raziyallahu anhu) ko charpai par rakha gaya to log un ke gird hue, dua kartay thay aur tareef kartay thay aur janaza uthaye janay se pehle un par dua kartay thay. Main bhi un logon mein tha. Main nahi dara magar aik shakhs se jis ne mera kandha mere peechay se thaam liya tha, main ne dekha to wo Ali (raziyallahu anhu) thay. Pas unhon ne Umar (raziyallahu anhu) ke liye Allah Taala se rehmat ki dua ki aur kaha ke Ae Umar! Tum ne koi shakhs aisa na chhora jis ke aamaal aisay hon ke waisay aamaal par mujhe Allah se milna pasand ho. Aur Allah ki qasam main ye samajhta tha ke Allah tumhein tumharay donon saathiyon ke saath karay ga, yani Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) aur Abu Bakr Siddiq (raziyallahu anhu), aur us ki wajah ye hai ke main aksar Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) se suna karta tha, Aap farmatay thay ke main aaya aur Abu Bakr aur Umar aaye aur main andar gaya aur Abu Bakr aur Umar gaye aur main nikla aur Abu Bakr aur Umar niklay. Is liye mujhe ummeed thi ke Allah Taala tumhein un donon ke saath karay ga. (Muslim: 7/111-112). Baab: Siddiq (raziyallahu anhu) ko janasheen banana."
"1626","[AI-translation] Ibn Abu Mulaika se riwayat hai, main ne Aisha (raziyallahu anha) se suna jabke un se poocha gaya ke Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) kise janasheen banatay agar banatay? Unhon ne kaha: Abu Bakr. To un se kaha gaya: Phir Abu Bakr ke baad kaun? Unhon ne kaha: Umar. Phir un se kaha gaya: Umar ke baad kaun? Unhon ne kaha: Abu Ubaida bin Jarrah. Phir wo is par ruk gayeen. (Muslim: 7/110)"
"1627","[AI-translation] Muhammad bin Jubair bin Mutim se, apne walid se riwayat hai ke aik aurat ne Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) se cheez maangi. To Aap ne usay hukm diya ke wo Aap ke paas wapas aaye. To us ne kaha: Ae Allah ke Rasool! Bataiye, agar main aayi aur Aap ko na paun? Un ke walid ne kaha ke goya wo maut murad leti thin. Aap ne farmaya: Phir agar tum mujhe na pao to Abu Bakr ke paas aana. (Muslim: 7/110)"
"1628","[AI-translation] Aisha (raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Mujh se Rasoolullah (sallallahu alaihi wa sallam) ne apne marz mein farmaya: Mere liye Abu Bakr, tumharay walid aur tumharay bhai ko bulao taake main kitab likhun. Beshak mujhe khauf hai ke koi tamanna karnay wala tamanna karay aur koi kehnay wala kahay ke main zyada haqdar hun. Aur Allah aur momin Abu Bakr ke siwa inkar kartay hain. (Muslim: 7/110). Baab: Umar bin Khattab (raziyallahu anhu) ki fazilat."
